# M9 timing-leg output config.
#
# The compiled-in default (no FESOM_IO_CONFIG) writes MONTHLY means for every default
# variable — ~600 MB per leg on CORE2, which across the fleet (cells x K x reps x node
# counts x CPU/GPU) is tens of GB of NetCDF nobody reads, plus per-step accumulation
# inside the timed loop.
#
# Timing legs therefore write one small 2-D field. This is common-mode across every cell,
# so it cannot bias an A/B; it just stops the fleet from filling /work.
#
# ⚠️ NOT for trajectory (L3) legs — those need the ice fields to diff. Use the default
#    config (unset FESOM_IO_CONFIG) or an explicit ice-variable config there.
sst     monthly
